# PART 5. BILINGUAL SYSTEM – HỆ THỐNG SONG NGỮ

This is a mandatory feature.

The entire application must support:

1. Vietnamese.
2. English.

Vietnamese must be the default language for first-time users.

Place a visible language switcher in the application header:

[VI] / [EN]

When users switch languages:
- All navigation labels must change.
- All buttons must change.
- All headings must change.
- All onboarding questions must change.
- All notifications must change.
- All error messages must change.
- All settings must change.
- All challenge descriptions must change.
- All system-generated interface messages must change.

Do not translate only the homepage.

Use a centralized internationalization system such as i18next or an equivalent dictionary-based localization system.

Remember the user's language preference after they leave and return.

The language switch must not reset user data, progress or account settings.

AI-generated content should respond in the language currently selected by the user.

