# PART 17. DESIGN AND UX QUALITY STANDARDS

Follow these principles:

### Hick's Law
Avoid overwhelming users with too many choices at once.

### Fitts's Law
Make important buttons large and easy to tap.

### Jakob's Law
Use familiar navigation and interaction patterns.

### Cognitive Load
Present information progressively.

### Feedback
Every meaningful action must provide clear feedback.

### Consistency
Use consistent colors, typography, icons and interaction patterns.

### Accessibility
Support keyboard navigation, readable text and appropriate contrast.

The application must feel simple even though it offers many features.

